        <name>Locale</name>
        <qualifiedname>UTryllRuntimeSettings::Locale</qualifiedname>
        <initializer>= TEXT(&quot;en&quot;)</initializer>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Session language as a BCP-47 tag (&quot;de&quot;, &quot;de-DE&quot;, &quot;pt-BR&quot;). One setting the whole voice + text stack derives from, so a language menu does not have to reach into every agent:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>TTS : the default tts_lang for every GenerateAndSpeak/Speak node (a node that authored its own TtsLang still wins).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>STT : language hint for multilingual recognizers (Whisper, Canary).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Files : node storage paths prefer loc/&lt;locale&gt;/ siblings when they exist, so localized knowledge bases and canned lines are a folder layout rather than code.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Text : templates can read the <computeroutput>language</computeroutput> key to write a &quot;reply in X&quot; instruction.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Empty leaves every one of those at its pre-locale behaviour. This is the value used at session start; to change language later call <ref refid="class_u_tryll_subsystem_1a8e74c44cd261eb57bcc774e646e83a0f" kindref="member">UTryllSubsystem::SetSessionLocale</ref>, which reaches existing agents&apos; voice and template keys but not content already bound to a node. FInternationalization::Get().GetCurrentCulture()-&gt;GetName() is the usual source. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
