        <qualifiedname>UTryllRuntimeSettings::GetLocaleOptions</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Choices for the Locale dropdown: the languages the project&apos;s <emphasis>registered</emphasis> models declare (<ref refid="class_u_tryll_model_manifest" kindref="compound">UTryllModelManifest</ref>), never a hardcoded list - so the menu can only ever offer something the project can actually load. Plus an empty entry, because &quot;no session language&quot; is a meaningful choice rather than a missing value.</para>
<para>A <bold>union</bold> across registered models, not an intersection: registering an English-only model for one character must not collapse the whole menu to English. Per-model mismatches surface on the model picker and at agent creation, where they are actionable.</para>
<para><bold>Fallback, not the primary path.</bold> In the editor, FTryllRuntimeSettingsCustomization replaces this row with a combo that annotates each entry with a catalog model count (&quot;German (de) - 7 models&quot;) while still storing the bare code. GetOptions cannot do that: it writes the <emphasis>selected string</emphasis> into the property, so an annotated entry would be stored as the locale. This stays for any surface that renders the property without that customization. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
